<title>USA: Pathmark Q3 net falls.</title>
<headline>Pathmark Q3 net falls.</headline>
<dateline>WOODBRIDGE, N.J. 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>PATHMARK STORES INC.</p>
<p>				(Dollars in Millions)</p>
<p>			    13 Weeks Ended	   39 Weeks Ended</p>
<p>			  11/2/96  10/28/95	11/2/96   10/28/95</p>
<p> Sales(a)		$ 973.8  $ 991.9    $ 2,929.5  $ 3,045.6</p>
<p> Operating earnings     34.4     33.0	  104.4	117.9</p>
<p>Gain on disposition</p>
<p>of freestanding</p>
<p>   drug stores		--	 --	     --	 15.5</p>
<p> Interest expense     (40.3)   (40.4)	(120.6)    (123.3)</p>
<p>Earnings (loss)</p>
<p>   before taxes	  (5.9)    (7.4)	 (16.2)	 10.1</p>
<p> Income tax benefit	2.3	3.7	    6.3     5.0(b)</p>
<p>Net earnings (loss)</p>
<p>before extraordinary</p>
<p>   item		    (3.6)    (3.7)	  (9.9)	 15.1</p>
<p>Extraordinary item,</p>
<p>   net of tax(c)	    --	 --	  (0.9)	   --</p>
<p> Net earnings (loss)  ( 3.6)   ( 3.7)	( 10.8)	 15.1</p>
<p>(a)  Includes sales generated by the freestanding drug stores of $11.2 million in the third quarter of fiscal 1995 and $97.7 million in the nine-month period of fiscal 1995. During the second quarter of fiscal 1995, Pathmark decided to dispose of its 36 freestanding drug stores and, on July 28, 1995, completed the sale of 30 of its drug stores to Rite Aid Corp.  Five of the remaining six drug stores were closed during fiscal 1995 and the sixth store, which generated sales of $0.4 million during fiscal 1996, closed in the second quarter of fiscal 1996. (b)  The fiscal 1995 income tax benefit includes a reversal of the deferred tax valuation allowance of $9.1 million for the 39 weeks ended Oct. 28, 1995. (c)  Represents loss on early extinguishment of debt.</p>
</text>
